# CVE-2026-14257: npm CLI's own bundled brace-expansion (5.0.7, at
# usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/brace-expansion) needs 5.0.8.
# This is inside the node:22-alpine base image's npm installation, not our
# application's dependency tree -- no published npm release ships the fix
# yet (checked 2026-07-31: npm@latest is 12.0.2, still bundles 5.0.7).
# Remove this line once npm publishes a release with brace-expansion >= 5.0.8.
CVE-2026-14257

# CVE-2026-69152: same npm CLI bundled brace-expansion (5.0.7) as above, a
# second CVE disclosed against the same unfixed version. Needs >= 1.1.18,
# 2.1.4, 3.0.6, or 5.0.9. Same base-image constraint applies (checked
# 2026-08-07: npm@latest is still 12.0.2, still bundles 5.0.7).
# Remove this line once npm publishes a release with brace-expansion >= 5.0.9
# (or the relevant fixed line).
CVE-2026-69152

# CVE-2026-69192: npm CLI's own bundled ip-address (10.2.0, pulled in via
# usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/socks/node_modules/ip-address)
# needs 10.3.1. Not in our application's dependency tree -- absent from
# package-lock.json entirely. Same base-image constraint as above (checked
# 2026-08-07: npm@latest is still 12.0.2, still bundles ip-address 10.2.0).
# Remove this line once npm publishes a release with ip-address >= 10.3.1.
CVE-2026-69192
